Dear Shelley

Thank you for your patience, and yes, the visit went well. Abel completed a full RF survey of the property, and I have attached our proposal based on that work.

In short, we are recommending that Barefoot Addo owns its own private wireless network rather than continuing to rent one. The proposal covers:

- What we found on site, including the current mounting structure and the gap at the spa
- The proposed build: a new engineered mast, two sector radios and 28 connection points, the spa included
- Why reliability matters here: guest experience, day-to-day operations, and after-hours security, engineered to 99.9% availability
- The investment, with the full scope of what is included
- The financial case, measured against what the lodge is spending today
- The order of work, and why the Vodacom link goes in last

This is offered on a 36-month agreement. I should also mention that we have secured the equipment for this build with our supplier, and wireless stock does tighten at this time of year - no pressure intended, just so you have the full picture.

I would welcome the chance to walk the owners through it, whether in person or by video call, as I know they are not based locally.

Please let me know if there is anything you would like clarified, or if it would help to have the numbers in a spreadsheet as well.

